{
  "duration": 81.599,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.28,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.799,
      "end": 1.759,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.419,
      "end": 3.559,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.339,
      "end": 5.099,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.659,
      "end": 7.46,
      "text": "we are given that a cyclist rides"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.0,
      "end": 9.26,
      "text": "thirty-five kilometer"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.84,
      "end": 10.8,
      "text": "in one hour"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.279,
      "end": 12.259,
      "text": "twenty-four minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.799,
      "end": 15.819,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the average speed of the cyclist."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.239,
      "end": 16.739,
      "text": "Now, first,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.239,
      "end": 18.959,
      "text": "let us note down the given values."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.52,
      "end": 20.899,
      "text": "Distance covered is thirty-five"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.359,
      "end": 21.919,
      "text": "kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.639,
      "end": 25.119,
      "text": "Time taken is one hour twenty-four minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.559,
      "end": 26.859,
      "text": "But be very sure about one thing,"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.42,
      "end": 29.539,
      "text": "the speed is asked in kilometer per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.039,
      "end": 35.219,
      "text": "while the time is given in hours and minutes. So before using the formula, we must first convert the time into hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.599,
      "end": 42.959,
      "text": "We know that one hour is equal to sixty minutes, so twenty-four minutes is equal to twenty-four divided by sixty hours,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.299,
      "end": 46.179,
      "text": "which is equal to two by five hour, and we already have one hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.659,
      "end": 49.0,
      "text": "So total time is equal to one plus two-fifths."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.319,
      "end": 51.919,
      "text": "That is equal to seven-fifths hours. Got it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.459,
      "end": 52.779,
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.259,
      "end": 54.579,
      "text": "Now, we know the basic formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.979,
      "end": 61.399,
      "text": "average speed is equal to total distance divided by total time. Putting the values, average speed is equal to thirty-five"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.879,
      "end": 63.219,
      "text": "divided by seven by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.539,
      "end": 66.259,
      "text": "Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.639,
      "end": 70.699,
      "text": "So thirty-five divided by seven by five becomes thirty-five into five by seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.18,
      "end": 74.119,
      "text": "After simplifying this, we get twenty-five kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.619,
      "end": 77.299,
      "text": "So the average speed of the cyclist is twenty-five"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.659,
      "end": 77.879,
      "text": "kilometer"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.559,
      "end": 81.599,
      "text": "per hour. Hence, the correct answer is option A."
    }
  ],
